            <div class="product-accordion">
  <div class="section opened">
    <h3 class="title">Information</h3>
    <div class="content product-description rte" itemprop="description">
      <p><p>This book collects the many individual sheets of the original 1965 British Rail Corporate Identity Manual into a unique singular volume </p>
<ul>
<li>Foreword by Michael C Place, creative director and founder of Build.</li>
<li>Introduction by Tony Howard, former head of design at British Rail, now managing director of Transport Design Consultancy.</li>
<li>Interview with Gerry Barney, designer of the British Rail double arrow symbol.</li>
<li>Essay from James Greenfield, creative director &amp; founder of Koto.</li>
<li>Essay from Dr Paul Rennie, writer and Context Subject Leader at Central Saint Martins.</li>
</ul></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  
    <div class="section">
      <h3 class="title">Print Specification</h3>
      <div class="content">
        
        <p>130gsm Lessebo Design</p>
        
        <p>2 Colour Foil Cover</p>
        
        <p>252 Photographic images</p>
        
        <p>310 x 247mm</p>
        
        <p>372pp</p>
        
        <p>5 throwout pages</p>
        
        <p>Buckram Cloth Cover</p>
        
        <p>CMYK with 2 spot colours</p>
        
        <p>H-UV Litho printed</p>
        
        <p>Hardback</p>
        
      </div>
    </div>
  

  
  <div class="section">
    <h3 class="title">Shipping & Returns</h3>
    <div class="content"><p>We offer worldwide shipping which is calculated at the checkout. All of our orders ship from the UK. To learn more see our <a href="https://britishrailmanual.myshopify.com/pages/shipping-returns">shipping & returns page</a>. </p></div>
  </div>
  
</div>
          

          
